12123	{"artifactId":"LLD-00d80121c593053c-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-00d80121c593053c-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-15T08:57:30.430Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reviewer's feedback (click a diff section to open the file at the relevant line) is designed. It is contract 2.2, migration step 4, ac5 and its tests. The non-goal (fenced code blocks in replies sharing the highlighter) is not built.","evidence":"Section 2.2 defines the open-code-ref click from the line and from the header path. Section 9 leaves fenced code blocks to a follow-up. The markdown path (render-registry.ts:435, marked.parse into innerHTML) is not touched by any step. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each diff line today is a div with a number span, a sign span and one text span set as plain text. The number is the old-side number for a removed line and the new-side number otherwise. A '\\' line is a note.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:567-572: `dEl('span','insrc-diffw__num',note?'':String(c==='-'?oldNo:newNo))` ... `dEl('span','insrc-diffw__text',note?l:l.slice(1))`; `if(c==='-')oldNo++;else if(c==='+')newNo++;else if(!note){oldNo++;newNo++;}`. So at a removed line newNo is the number the next new-side line takes, which matches the design's rule for line numbers. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The page's only library is marked. It comes from a generated string (webview-marked.ts, written by gen-webview-libs.mjs from a prebuilt file) inlined in the one nonce'd script, under a CSP of default-src 'none' with nonce-only scripts.","evidence":"gen-webview-libs.mjs:18 reads `node_modules/marked/marked.min.js` and writes `MARKED_SRC`. chat-panel.ts:924: `default-src 'none'; img-src data:; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'nonce-${nonce}';`. chat-panel.ts:1419: `<script nonce=\"${nonce}\">${MARKED_SRC}\\n;${bootstrap}</script>`. [files: vscode-plugin/gen-webview-libs.mjs, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host opens a clicked code reference from the first workspace folder. It refuses absent, '..', outside or non-existent paths with a log, and opens in the review pane's group, else beside the chat.","evidence":"extension.ts:625 `root: () => vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders?.[0]?.uri.fsPath`. extension.ts:629 `viewColumn: reviewColumn() ?? vscode.ViewColumn.Beside`. link-opener.ts:57-70 warns and returns on no root, a non-string path, '..', or resolveWithin returning undefined, and it never throws (link-opener.ts:73). [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-opener.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The open-code-ref message, the host handler in chat-panel and the registry's link-open sink (onLinkOpen / LDEC, wired to postMessage) already exist and can be reused without a new message.","evidence":"protocol.ts:306 `{ readonly type: 'open-code-ref'; readonly path: string; readonly line?: number | undefined }`. chat-panel.ts:2039-2040 `case 'open-code-ref': ... links.openCodeRef(msg.path, msg.line)`. render-registry.ts:363 `var LDEC=null;function onLinkOpen(cb){LDEC=cb;}`. chat-panel.ts:1244 `reg.onLinkOpen(function(p){vs.postMessage({v:1,payload:p});})`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The token colour names exist in the :root layer of chat-panel.ts as VS Code theme variables: --magenta, --accent, --amber, --user, --accent2, --muted and --link.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:961 `--accent:var(--vscode-terminal-ansiGreen);--accent2:var(--vscode-terminal-ansiCyan);--amber:var(--vscode-terminal-ansiYellow);--magenta:var(--vscode-terminal-ansiMagenta);--user:var(--vscode-terminal-ansiBlue);`. chat-panel.ts:950-951 define --muted and --link. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No highlighter is bundled today, and esbuild is already a devDependency the generator can use.","evidence":"package.json:793 `\"esbuild\": \"^0.28.1\"`. The only webview library dependency is `\"marked\": \"^4.3.0\"` (package.json:796). highlight.js does not appear in package.json, so adding it is new, and package.json is listed as a change site. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.4","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared fake DOM already has a text node, which the unit fixtures rely on.","evidence":"fake-dom.ts:86 `export function textNode(data: string): BodyStub` makes a nodeType-3 node. The getter at fake-dom.ts:123 `get textContent() { return txt; }` does not join children, which confirms the design's statement that it must change. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-dom.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"renderRegistryWebviewSource is consumed only by chat-panel.ts, so the review pane gets no highlighter and its page is unchanged.","evidence":"A grep of the non-test sources finds renderRegistryWebviewSource imported only at chat-panel.ts:16 and used at chat-panel.ts:1237. docs-review-panel.ts imports MARKED_SRC (line 20) but not the render registry. Listing docs-review-panel.ts under 'Call sites' while calling it unchanged is only an over-listing. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Optionally drop docs-review-panel.ts from the call-site list, or mark it as read-only.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A click on the header path posts open-code-ref and does not toggle, while the rest of the header still toggles. The header's toggle listener is the site to change.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:583 `head.addEventListener('click',toggle)`. The delegated document handler (render-registry.ts:364) runs after the head listener as the click bubbles up. So the postcondition that a path click does not toggle requires the head handler to skip path clicks, and step 4 states this. The head has a toggle only when hidden>0 (line 577 returns earlier otherwise). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"When building, make the head's toggle ignore clicks whose target is inside .insrc-diffw__path. The order of the document handler alone will not prevent the toggle.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test suites affected by the change are named: chat-shell.test.ts (shared fake, diff rows on .ts paths, document stub without createTextNode) and render-registry.test.ts (its own fake, no highlighter global, so it stays on the plain path).","evidence":"chat-shell.test.ts:19 imports from './fake-dom.js'. chat-shell.test.ts:98 has `document: { getElementById, createElement: ..., addEventListener }`, with no createTextNode. Its diff rows use 'src/a.ts' (line 391). render-registry.test.ts:56-57 has its own `fakeDocument()` with only createElement, and its diff assertions read `insrc-diffw__text` textContent (lines 1158, 1255). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/render-registry.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DiffSection and the stored diff row are unchanged. Highlighting and the click data are derived in the page from the existing path, lines and newStart, so stored rows work unchanged.","evidence":"diff-sections.ts:23-25 shows that DiffSection carries `path`, and the section construction at diff-sections.ts:234 carries `path, oldStart, oldLines, newStart, newLines, added, removed, lines`. fillDiff already reads path, lines and newStart from the row (render-registry.ts:559-566). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/diff-sections.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A bundled highlighter text containing '<script' or '</script' would break the shell's single-script checks. The design detects this in the generator and fails the build.","evidence":"chat-shell.test.ts:331 `assert.equal((on.match(/<script\\b/g) ?? []).length, 1)`. chat-panel.test.ts:1784 has 'exactly one inline script'. chat-shell.test.ts:61 extracts the script up to `html.lastIndexOf('</script>')`. A literal script tag in the inlined string would break these and the browser parse, which justifies the escape-and-fail step. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/gen-webview-libs.mjs]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A refused click (a deleted file, or a folder that is not the first workspace folder) is detected by the host and logged, and nothing happens in the page.","evidence":"link-opener.ts:66-69: `const real = await resolveWithin(root, path, fs); if (real === undefined) { deps.log.warn(...not a file inside the workspace); return; }`. The page gets no reply, so the widget is unchanged. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-opener.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each derived criterion ac1-ac5 maps to at least one named test. The theme test that ac2 relies on has an exact added-selector list and forbids --vscode- in RENDER_REGISTRY_STYLE, so adding the selectors to the inline list is the right change.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping in section 5 covers ac1-ac5. chat-theme.test.ts:157 `assert.ok(!RENDER_REGISTRY_STYLE.includes('--vscode-'))`. chat-theme.test.ts:327 'the added selectors are exactly the listed ones' with an inline list (lines 354-366 include .insrc-diffw*). It reads chat-theme-before.json as the frozen fixture (line 328). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-theme.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-15T08:57:30.430Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
